    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on October 11, our offensive production is severely stifled by a difficult matchup against Misiorowski, whose 2.35 xERA renders our primary bats marginal at best. **Kyle Tucker** (47.89) remains our most viable starter in the outfield, though his score is significantly suppressed by the combination of an elite arm and an unfavorable #8 spot in the order. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (43.07) anchors the UTIL slot; while his matchup against the right-handed Misiorowski is neutral, he lacks the ceiling to elevate beyond the \"marginal\" tier today. Given that Stolen Bases are our most scarce category, the lack of elite speed options on the active slate makes this a day to focus on minimizing damage to our cumulative stats rather than chasing high-upside production.\n\nThe decision to bench **Luis Lara** (33.85) was the most nuanced call of the morning. While **Luis Lara** possesses the switch-hitting versatility that usually provides a floor-raising platoon advantage, his projection was crushed by a brutal matchup against Skubal (2.85 xERA). With a sub-40 score failing to meet our organizational efficiency threshold, we opted to protect our game caps rather than force an inferior asset against an elite southpaw. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL, while the absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**\u2014both currently serving team off-days\u2014leave our middle-order depth looking dangerously thin for this 5x5 Roto stretch. With no weather-related risks flagged, our strategy remains defensive, waiting for a more favorable pitching environment for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, and the rest of our core.",
